\chapter*{Glossary of Key Terms}
\begin{multicols}{2}
\begin{description}
\item[Analytic Rank] The order of vanishing of an L-function at the central point.
\item[Betti Number] The rank of the $n$-th homology group of a topological space.
\item[Conjecture] A mathematical statement believed to be true but not yet proven.
\item[Differential Form] A mathematical object used in multivariable calculus and topology.
\item[Elliptic Curve] A smooth projective curve of genus 1 with a specified rational point.
\item[Fundamental Group] The group of homotopy classes of loops based at a point.
\item[Group Representation] A homomorphism from a group to the general linear group.
\item[Homology] An algebraic invariant associating sequences of abelian groups to a space.
\item[L-Function] A complex function encoding arithmetic information about number-theoretic objects.
\item[Manifold] A topological space locally homeomorphic to Euclidean space.
\item[Modular Form] A holomorphic function on the upper half-plane satisfying transformation laws.
\item[Moduli Space] A geometric space whose points correspond to isomorphism classes of mathematical objects.
\item[Ricci Flow] A geometric evolution equation smoothing Riemannian metrics.
\item[Sphere Packing] The problem of arranging non-overlapping identical spheres in space.
\item[Topology] The study of properties preserved under continuous deformations.
\item[Vector Field] An assignment of a vector to each point in a space.
\item[Weil--Petersson Metric] A natural Riemannian metric on the moduli space of Riemann surfaces.
\end{description}
\end{multicols}

